MetroFuse Deezer provider, GPL-3.0-or-later.

This separate provider targets MetroFuse API 1.1.0 and the matching plugin SDK.
Build and account-screen patterns follow the MetroFuse YouTube Music reference:
https://github.com/956tris/MetroFuse-YouTube-Music

The desktop package includes the self-contained Windows WebView2 sign-in
helper from the matching MetroFuse plugin SDK (GPL-3.0-or-later):
https://github.com/956tris/MetroFuse/tree/8d62892c04be53e84956390f5dee1f90bf082706/plugin-sdk/windows-webview
It is extracted from the compile-time SDK JAR into this plugin's desktop
assets. Its request, profile and process lifecycle are owned by this plugin.
The helper is excluded from the Android package.

Deezer gateway request and media response shapes were inspected in deezer-py
1.3.7 and the user's dzmedia-metrofuse Rust service. This plugin implements its
own Kotlin session, catalog, Home, library and range-streaming logic. It does
not bundle or run dzmedia, deezer-py or another provider's account credentials.

Library, playlist, Home, account media and FLAC_24 request contracts were also
compared with LuftVerbot's Echo Deezer extension at commit
d67083dc5c7cc4ca939f17d659ed350d3199bb3d:
https://github.com/LuftVerbot/echo-deezer-extension/tree/d67083dc5c7cc4ca939f17d659ed350d3199bb3d
No Echo runtime or source files are bundled. Live endpoint verification and
the supported music-library scope are documented in docs/endpoints.md in this
plugin's source repository.

All fixture identities, tokens and audio bytes are synthetic. Signed URLs,
account cookies and license tokens are kept in memory and never logged or
written to plugin settings or ordinary storage. Browser session persistence
belongs to the host's encrypted credential store.
